The files are the report, written: one `demo.toml` marked `draft = true`
with `compat = "none"` and no `since`, a `types.toml` and the schema sidecars.
A draft never overwrites — the file a reviewer is halfway through is exactly
the one an overwrite would destroy — so a second run into the same directory
is refused whole, exit 2, before a byte is written.

```console
$ zenctl registry infer --from fixture.zrec --out draft --format json
? 2
Error: --out draft already holds 6 file(s) this run would write (demo.toml, types.toml, schemas/DemoBoom.json…) — a draft never overwrites; pick an empty directory

```

`--for` is a live window; a capture's span is in its rows.

```console
$ zenctl registry infer --from fixture.zrec --for 5 --out draft2 --format json
? 2
Error: --for is a live window; a capture's span is in its rows — drop one of the two

```

The loop closes on `registry lint`: the build lint refuses a draft (exit 1,
a finding — `zenkey-build` says the same), and `--allow-drafts` admits it
for prototyping, as a warning every build sees.

```console
$ zenctl registry lint draft
? 1
Error: registry lint failed [demo]: declares draft = true — an observation-derived, unreviewed registry (RFC 08 §6.1). Review it, drop the marker and add `since` to promote it; or build with Config::allow_drafts() to prototype against it

```

```console
$ zenctl registry lint --allow-drafts draft
{"dir":"draft","notes":[{"text":"demo draft — observation-derived and unreviewed (RFC 08 §6.1): admitted by allow_drafts, unpinned, every field a guess; promote it by review"}],"passed":true,"report":"registry-lint","warnings":["demo draft — observation-derived and unreviewed (RFC 08 §6.1): admitted by allow_drafts, unpinned, every field a guess; promote it by review"]}
demo draft — observation-derived and unreviewed (RFC 08 §6.1): admitted by allow_drafts, unpinned, every field a guess; promote it by review

```
